> "You make black scratch marks on the stone"

There are several different kinds of gray stone, and only a blessed
touchstone will identify gems (unless you are an archaeologist or a
gnome, in which case an uncursed touchstone will do).  I can tell that
your stone is not a touchstone, because a worthless piece of glass
would have left *colourless* scratch marks on an uncursed touchstone,
and a real gem would have left coloured streaks.

You sound relatively unspoiled, so here are two important things to
remember about gray stones.  Kick any gray stone you find before
picking it up to make sure it's not a loadstone (which weighs a ton
and sticks to you), and keep cursed gray stones stashed away until you
can uncurse them.  If you want to be thoroughly spoiled, take a look
at http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/343/gems-343.html
